We have the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
4u - 5v &= 23 \quad \text{(1)} \\
2u + 4v &= -8 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}

First, we'll solve equation (2) for $u$:
\begin{align*}
2u + 4v &= -8 \\
2u &= -8 - 4v \\
u &= -4 - 2v
\end{align*}

Next, we substitute $u = -4 - 2v$ into equation (1):
\begin{align*}
4(-4 - 2v) - 5v &= 23 \\
-16 - 8v - 5v &= 23 \\
-16 - 13v &= 23 \\
-13v &= 39 \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}

Now, we substitute $v = -3$ back into the expression for $u$:
\begin{align*}
u &= -4 - 2(-3) \\
u &= -4 + 6 \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $u + v$ is:
\begin{align*}
u + v &= 2 + (-3) \\
u + v &= -1
\end{align*}

The final answer is $\boxed{-1}$.
